  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CE1GW4B8000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "treeview.md",
    "text": "**Stale `TreeView.unfolds` references have no general cleanup**: `TreeView.unfold(ref)` appends with no existence check, and the only cleanup — a reactive strip-on-hard-delete — only fires at the exact moment a specific id is hard-deleted; nothing revisits an *existing* `unfolds` entry against what's currently live. Confirmed live: `.state/TreeView.jsonld`'s `default` view has named 10 `BlockNode` ids with no corresponding document at all, after unrelated reconciliation churn elsewhere reassigned/removed the blocks those ids used to name. See [Settled](../discussion/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1FFSR8006) for the chosen fix direction.",
    "parent": "FolderNode:00CDBYV4BR003",
    "type": "root",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CE1GW638001"
    ],
    "path": "issues/treeview.md",
    "fileHash": "9bbe74670fc83184aa01af385f5ee669158957e2c19f00e240be1606abf0fe90",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-09-11T08:17:42.445Z",
    "ingestedHash": "9bbe74670fc83184aa01af385f5ee669158957e2c19f00e240be1606abf0fe90",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-09-11T08:20:32.159Z",
    "projectedHash": "9bbe74670fc83184aa01af385f5ee669158957e2c19f00e240be1606abf0fe90"
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CE1GW4B8001",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "treeview.md",
    "text": "Fix the treeview-specific gaps and the two relocated ingest/parser gaps together, since they were bundled by direct instruction rather than filed separately. No particular cross-dependency between them — order by whichever's simplest to verify in isolation.",
